## {{ n + 9 }}. Propose an action

```python
fidelity = get("/fidelity").json()["state"]          # what the interlock will judge by
types = get("/actions").json()
for a in types["data"]:
    print(a["id"], a["control"], a["autonomy"], a["bounds"], a["binding"], a["executable"])

response = client.post("/actions/<action>/propose",
                       json={"object": "<uid>", "params": {"value": "<number>"},
                             "reason": "<why>", "source": "<your name>"},
                       headers={"Idempotency-Key": str(uuid.uuid4())})
proposal = response.json()
if response.status_code == 422:                      # refused, and recorded as rejected
    print(proposal["code"], proposal["errors"], proposal["record"])
else:
    record = checked(response).json()["data"]
    print(record["uid"], record["status"], record["fidelity"], record["reasons"])
    record = get(f"/actions/records/{record['uid']}").json()["data"]
    print(record["approval"], record["execution"], record["reconciliation"], record["observed"])
```

- `status` `proposed`: advice only, or waiting for a person's approval. Give the user the record's uid and stop; approving is the user's (`POST /actions/records/{uid}/approve` with `by` the user, only when the user says so for that record).
- `status` `blocked`: the interlock refused it in the twin's present state. Final: never work around it; tell the user why.
- `status` `executed`: the call was made; `execution` holds its HTTP status and when it takes effect. `reconciliation` becomes `ok` or `mismatch` once its settle time has passed and a sync run has read the result.
- `status` `failed`: the call failed; `execution` says how. Do not propose it again in a loop; report it.
- The same `Idempotency-Key` with the same proposal gives back the same record (200); a new proposal needs a new key.
